<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Locke returns for his preventive visit, having turned 60 last week. He completed the health risk questionnaire beforehand. His asthma has been steady in the three months since tiotropium was added: he uses one or two extra inhalations of budesonide-formoterol a week, sleeps through the night, and has had no flare. The dose counters show no missed maintenance doses. He finished pulmonary rehabilitation in the spring and keeps up the walking program five days a week. The open fires in his rooms have stayed out of use, and the HEPA air cleaner runs in his study and bedroom. He spent four days in the city last month, checked the air quality index each morning, and needed his reliever twice. He has had no fever, weight loss, night sweats, or blood in his sputum. He had a normal colonoscopy eight years ago. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Preventive health visit, age 60</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Asthma with persistent airflow limitation on budesonide-formoterol maintenance and reliever with add-on tiotropium; exposure to air pollution</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Budesonide-formoterol 160/4.5 mcg two inhalations twice daily plus as needed; tiotropium 2.5 mcg two inhalations daily</td></tr><tr><td>Screening history</td><td>Normal colonoscopy eight years ago; HIV, hepatitis B, and hepatitis C tests negative in his fifties</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, better than for many years</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with long-standing friends; busy with writing and his board work; no financial worries</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; wine a few evenings a week (AUDIT-C 2); walks 30 to 40 minutes five days a week; plain diet with fruit and vegetables most days</td></tr><tr><td>Environmental</td><td>No open fires in his rooms; HEPA air cleaner in study and bedroom; checks the air quality index before city trips</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms fitted; no firearms</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Not sexually active; no risk factors for sexually transmitted infection</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No hearing difficulty; reading glasses; eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Sleeps through the night; no snoring reported</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

