<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Preventive health visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a personalized prevention plan made. His chief risk is his chronic airway disease, now well managed, which makes the seasonal respiratory vaccines a priority. Lipids are normal and his estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk is below 7.5 percent. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Asthma with persistent airflow limitation (J45.40)</content>. Steady three months after adding tiotropium: reliever once or twice a week, no night symptoms, no flare; no inhaled-corticosteroid side effects. [S]<list><item>Continue budesonide-formoterol and tiotropium.</item><item>Asthma review with an Asthma Control Test as booked next month.</item><item>Influenza, COVID-19, and RSV vaccines today.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose given today; recommended at 60 to 74 with chronic lung disease</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended from 50; he preferred not to have a fourth injection today and will have dose 1 at his next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 given six months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal colonoscopy eight years ago; next due in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 182 mg/dL, HDL 64 mg/dL, LDL 101 mg/dL, triglycerides 85 mg/dL; blood pressure 120/74 mmHg; never smoker; no diabetes; estimated 10-year risk below 7.5 percent, so no statin</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 19.9 with no other risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>HIV, hepatitis B, and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>One-time tests negative in his fifties</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 2</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision about PSA screening at 55 to 69 discussed; he chose not to be screened this year</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker; CT this spring showed no nodules</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No concerns; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, this season&apos;s formula; Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine, single dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (2021); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Statin Use for the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults: Preventive Medication (2022); Prostate Cancer: Screening (2018); Lung Cancer: Screening (2021)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Asthma review next month as booked; zoster vaccine dose 1 then. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-22: asthma review two weeks after a cold with a yellow-zone flare. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 17 minutes, with his consent. He has not written a directive before. He names a long-standing friend in the household where he lives as his health care agent and took the state form to complete. He would want full treatment for any illness he might recover from, including a period on a ventilator for a severe asthma attack, and would not want his life prolonged by machines if he could not recover awareness. He asked that his health information be shared with his care team and his agent. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
